- <get geography_facts>

! array geography_facts = Russia spans 11 time zones|The Pacific Ocean is larger than all land areas combined|Mount Everest grows about 4 millimeters taller each year|The Dead Sea is actually a lake and the lowest point on Earth's surface|Antarctica is the world's largest desert|Alaska is the only US state in both Eastern and Western Hemispheres|The Amazon River has no bridges crossing it|Canada has more lakes than the rest of the world combined|Istanbul is the only city on two continents|The Sahara Desert is expanding southward|Vatican City has its own postal system and issues its own euros|Singapore is both a city and a country|The Nile River flows north|Africa is splitting apart slowly along the Great Rift Valley

+ fun geography facts
- Australia is wider than the Moon! Bangladesh has more people than Russia despite being 120 times smaller. Libya is 99% desert. The Netherlands has more museums per square mile than any other country. Chile is 2,600 miles long but averages only 110 miles wide.

+ geography records
- Longest river: Nile (4,132 miles). Largest lake: Caspian Sea. Deepest point: Mariana Trench (36,200 feet deep). Highest waterfall: Angel Falls, Venezuela (3,212 feet). Driest place: Atacama Desert, Chile.

+ countries and borders  
- China and Russia each border 14 countries (most of any country). Vatican City and San Marino are completely surrounded by Italy. Lesotho is completely surrounded by South Africa. France has the most time zones of any country (12).

+ island facts
- Indonesia has over 17,000 islands. Only about 6,000 are inhabited. Great Britain is the largest European island. Greenland is the world's largest island (not counting Australia as a continent). Madagascar is the 4th largest island globally.